---
title: "FIG. 5 — FEC Block Lifecycle State Machine"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ACCUMULATING: First source symbol received

    ACCUMULATING: State 504<br/>Counting source symbols<br/>Timer T running
    DECODING: State 505<br/>FEC decoder invoked<br/>Awaiting sufficient symbols
    CLEAN: State 501 ✓<br/>All K source arrived<br/>No FEC needed
    RECOVERED: State 502 ✓<br/>FEC decode succeeded<br/>< K source + repair >= K
    FAILED: State 503 ✗<br/>Timeout expired<br/>Insufficient symbols

    ACCUMULATING --> CLEAN: K source symbols\nreceived (504b)
    ACCUMULATING --> DECODING: Repair symbol arrives\nwith < K source (504c)
    ACCUMULATING --> FAILED: Timer T expires (505a)
    DECODING --> RECOVERED: Decode succeeds\nsource + repair >= K
    DECODING --> FAILED: Timer T expires (505a)

    note right of ACCUMULATING
        Timer T = (D / fps) * safety_multiplier * 1000 ms
        D = interleave depth in frames
        fps = detected frame rate
        safety_multiplier = 3.0 (default)
    end note

    note left of CLEAN
        Terminal states add SBN to
        completed-blocks set.
        Late symbols for completed
        blocks are discarded.
    end note

    note right of FAILED
        greenFillFrames++
        Error concealment applied
    end note
